SUMMARY:Coaching Inclusion
DESCRIPTION:Why Inclusion is Good Business with Jane Horan Most leaders bel
 ieve their team is inclusive\, but their team often see it differently. Dr
 awing on case studies and coaching stories from Coaching Inclusion\, this 
 talk makes the business case for inclusion in plain terms: better decision
 s\, stronger retention\, and helping leaders access the full range of expe
 rtise in the room. The book and talk reframe inclusion as a daily leadersh
 ip practice\, and participants experience one of the key elements of inclu
 sion through a short listening and questioning exercise developed through 
 years of coaching leaders across industries and cultures. Walk-ins welcome
